# Markdown outside skills/ WAS excluded here for a few hours on 2026-09-15, because under the then-current proseWrap: preserve a pass over those files
# changed nothing but *em* -> _em_ and table padding — churn with no reading benefit at all. proseWrap is now `always` (see .prettierrc.yaml), which
# changes the trade completely: the pass now applies the 160-column convention to every doc in the tree, which is the thing that was wanted. So there is
# no markdown rule here any more. The named .md exclusions elsewhere in this file stand on their own reasons — .claude/DESIGN.md is byte-identical to
# another repo's copy, backlog/ is round-tripped by a single-writer tool, and the skills fixture holds item files rather than prose.

# The two stylesheets, byte-pinned the same way client/index.html is, just verified by source-text regex instead of a hash. Three suites read these
# files as TEXT rather than parsing them — test/project-hue.test.ts matches the literal selector `:root,[data-theme="midnight"]` to collect a theme's
# blocks, test/design-guards.test.ts checks §2.2's daylight values and the 11px type floor, and test/run-track-style.test.ts reads the reduced-motion
# and stalled rules. Measured 2026-09-15: a prettier pass turned that selector into `:root,\n[data-theme='midnight']` — a line break and single quotes
# — and took all three suites red, 12 cases in total, for no change to a single rendered pixel. The alternative was loosening three behaviour guards to
# tolerate whitespace, which trades a real check for a cosmetic diff; excluding the files keeps the guards strict and costs nothing.
shared/theme.css
client/src/styles.css

# The path-scoped rule files, excluded for a structural reason rather than a cosmetic one. Each body line in .claude/rules/ is ONE pointer — a sentence
# plus a single docs/subsystems/invariants.md anchor — and test/claude-rules.test.ts enforces that by requiring every non-heading line to contain that
# path, on the reasoning that a line which does not is a second copy of the rationale starting to grow. proseWrap: always has no way to know that: on
# 2026-09-15 it split orchestrator.md's 174-character pointer across two lines, leaving "- Before changing files here, read" alone on the first, which
# is exactly the shape the guard exists to reject. Nothing here is prose to be wrapped, so there is nothing for a width to improve.
.claude/rules/
